VALUES (578, '3', $t$ASK 578: the child reads the engine's Shared Library from the call; the child's own copy is removed$t$,
  $t$The child workflow (the second alternate pass) stores its own copy of the Shared Library, equal to the engine's. Every library change is written twice, and a run stops with pkgLIB1 if the two copies differ. Make the engine's copy the only one: the engine sends its library text in the one call it makes to the child, and the child's library readers read it from the call. Expected effect: one library write instead of two; the fault "engine and child libraries differ" can no longer occur; less stored in each child version. It does not make a run faster. No prompt, reasoning setting, model setting, check rule or output changes. (plan rev 3, section 1 OBJECTIVE, fairjudge/w3/a578/ASK578_plan_rev3.md md5 53fe3c1d)$t$,
  'in part',
  $t$Written by W4 at 19:08 CST 2026-11-24 on the operator's press, and read back MATCH by W1 (Wall 11851, 11852; audit 41852). Engine 634afc23 to 912dd47a, one node changed (Alternate Pass Call sends the field lib); child 85515391 to aad0ad9c, 14 readers and Library Check (ASK 422a) changed, the Shared Library node removed, 155 nodes. IN PART because the plan's DONE asks for the manual entry and two live runs in which the second alternate pass runs, and neither exists. SHOWN: C1 to C5 and C8 on the targets and on the fetch-backs (t578c, 22 checks, ALL PASS; standing set 31 PASS, 0 FAIL; pair check PASSES with the child's Library Check run on what the engine sends); C7 (a) and (b) by a one-time test workflow run on the operator's press (a 1,203,331-character text resolved and arrived whole; Wall 11752, 11753). NOT SHOWN: C6 (the readers' outputs on a real second alternate pass; the inputs cannot be rebuilt from stored rows, Wall 11744); C7 (c) (the real child execution's saved size and duration); the payload limit of the instance is NOT ESTABLISHED (the test call carried 1.2 MB, the real call about 9.1 MB; W1 N2). W1's N1: the pair check matches the Alternate Pass Call expression text and does not evaluate it, so the first live run that reaches the second alternate pass is the proof. Measured: the stored child shrinks from 1,422,386 to 97,905 characters; each child execution now stores the 1.28 MB library text once, about 6.7 percent of the one stored child execution read (42258, 18,981,883 bytes); the engine stores no item that holds the text (Wall 11848). Exception accepted by the grader: the engine's Alternate Pass Call carries no ASK 578 comment, because an n8n expression ends at the first "}}" (W1 N5, Wall 11850). After this write a Library change is made on the engine only. RUN REVISION 42528 (this row; where a sentence above says that no run has executed, that a path is unexercised, or what objective_met is, this paragraph is the later word): run ODV1-42528-dqwbcshc (debate_results e0e528d8, row saved 22:59 CST 2026-11-24; launch 22:26 CST, ended with success 23:42 CST; engine 2df7f6fa and child aad0ad9c by the write records; google/gemini-4-hydrogen as the Oracle defending against meta/muse-spark-1.3; every stage ran and no error row was written; outcome UNGRADED, panel 0-0 with 3 not counted under the debate rule; three judgments and 659 enforcer rows stored; cost 11.1907). The second alternate pass was called: call_costs holds "R2 Alternate Call openrouter" (anthropic/claude-sonnet-5.5, 1.0795) and enforcer row 54719 records its reply; debate_errors holds no "pkgLIB" text. W4 read child execution 42539 (Wall 11938): before the call two nodes read the library, Library Check (ASK 422a) and R2 Alternate Build, the second from the text the engine sent in the call. The alternate's reply was cut at its output limit (finish length, 64,000 tokens), so no child node after the call read the library: the 13 stubs and the pass's rows are NOT shown. W3 counts this run for the call only and NOT as one of the two live runs: a run counts when a second alternate's reply is read and processed. objective_met stays 'in part' and status 'read back'.$t$,
